t vehicles have 12-volt electrical systems, but there are some (like hybrid/electric vehicles) that are highly electrified and use higher voltage systems. Some older vehicles used less than 12-volt systems as well."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How to Test a Car Battery?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Testing an existing battery is critical to determining the remaining voltage left in the battery."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How to Use a Multimeter to Test a Car Battery?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can test your vehicle’s battery by using a multimeter, which tells you the voltage of your battery. Fully charged batteries should measure at 12.6 volts or above. When the engine is running, this measurement should be 13.7 to 14.7 volts.If you are uncertain about how your battery is performing, please visit one of our locations for a battery inspection today."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How to Tell if a Car Battery is Bad?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"There are telltale signs that can point to a bad battery. If you experience one of the following items, bring your vehicle contact and bring your car into one of our locations as soon as possible.\nSigns a Car Battery is Going Bad:\n Slowly Starting Car: Upon ignition, listen for the engine to be struggling to turn over. Illuminated Indicator Lights: Watch if the dashboard lights indicating the car’s charging system will be on at the time of ignition."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How to Clean Car Battery Terminals?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We recommend letting our professionals help you with your car battery, so schedule a battery service appointment at one of our locations if you think your battery is in need of a cleaning."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How to Charge a Car Battery?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We recommend letting our technicians help you with your car battery, so schedule an appointment at one of our locations if you think your battery is in need of a charge."}}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org/","@type":"WebSite","url":"index.html","potentialAction":{"@type":"SearchAction","target":{"@type":"EntryPoint","urlTemplate":"index.html?q={search_term_string"},"query-input":"required name=search_term_string"}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org/","@type":"Service","name":"Battery Replacement","brand":{"@type":"Brand","name":"Goodyear"},"description":"When your vehicle needs a new battery, our experts provide professional replacement using quality batteries designed to meet your vehicle’s needs. Proper installation helps ensure reliable starting power and dependable performance.","url":"-us/services/battery-replacement_211130/index.html","provider":{"@type":"LocalBusiness","name":"Goodyear"}}</script><!--$--><!--$--><!--/$--><div class="Services relative min-h-screen"><!--$--><!--/$--><div><div class="opacity-100"><div class="analytics-event-listener contents"></div></div><nav role="navigation" aria-label="Jump Navigation" class="w-full shadow-pdp-jumpnav bg-[#f4f4f4] fixed top-0 left-0 right-0 z-50
